summary:
Course registration challenges are not a new problem. For as long as there have been students, there’s been the stress of signing up for courses — figuring out when your registration window opens, and setting alarms and reminders to ensure you log in and pick out your classes before anyone else.&nbsp;
Not all students are lucky enough to get the classes they need, an issue that can be more prevalent at public institutions due to budget constraints and lack of faculty.
In the age of artificial intelligence and ever-advancing technology, these complications should be a thing of the past. And…
